        "title": "Lesson 1 | Bio of Imam Malik",
        "overview": "In this lesson, we delve into the life and legacy of Imām Mālik ibn Anas, one of the greatest scholars of Islām. Born in 93 AH, Imām Mālik grew up in a prominent family in Madīnah and became renowned for his deep knowledge of Ḥadīth and Fiqh. His contributions to Islamic jurisprudence are best encapsulated in his masterpiece, Al-Muwaṭṭāʾ, which remains one of the most respected collections of Ḥadīth. We explore his early years, his pursuit of knowledge, his notable teachers, such as al-Zuhrī and al-A'raj, and the rigorous discipline he employed in selecting authentic narrations.\n\nAdditionally, we discuss his profound respect for the Ḥadīth of the Prophet Muḥammad (PBUH), as well as anecdotes that highlight his unwavering commitment to preserving and teaching the prophetic traditions despite numerous challenges. Join us as we uncover the inspiring story of Imām Mālik and his enduring impact on Islamic scholarship.",
