        "title": "Lesson 1: The Definition of Fiqh and the Ahkām Taklīfiyyah",
        "overview": "In preparation for the Mukhtasar, our first lesson covers preliminary points regagrding the definition of Fiqh, the Ahkam Takleefiyyah, and role Qat' and Zann in the Hanafi understanding of proofs.\n\nThe definition of Fiqh is explained in detail, referring back to Mahbubi's Tanqeeh 'ala al-Tawdih and Mulla Khursu's Mir'ah upon the Mirqah. The Ahkam Takleefiyyah are then explained in light of Qat' and Zann, as well as the rule these two levels play in thuboot and dalalah, and how that effect's the Hanafi understanding of Fardhiyyah, Hurmah, and other categories.\n\nJoin our ‘Ibādāt course right now at https://talweehacademy.com/courses/mukhtasar-al-quduri-qism-al-ibadat/\n\nDon't forget the limited time offer available until Oct 31,2025 for both 'Ibadat and 'Uqubat with the coupon alquduri10 for $10 off/month!\n\nSign up today at: https://talweehacademy.com/",
