        "title": "Lesson 36 : Inna and its Sisters Continued",
        "overview": "In this video, we continue our discussion on the ḥurūf mushabbahah bi al-fi’l. When إن is mukhaffafah:\n\nWith jumlah fi‘liyyah, it never does ‘amal.\n\nWith jumlah ismiyyah, it rarely does ‘amal (e.g. إنْ كلُّ نفسٍ لما عليها حافظ).\n\nIf it doesn’t do ‘amal, the lām must appear in the khabar to distinguish it from negation.\n\nWhen أن is mukhaffafah:\nIt keeps its ‘amal but requires a hidden ḍamīr al-sha’n as its ism, and its khabar must be a full sentence — e.g. عَلِمَ أنْ سيكون.\nTo distinguish أنْ المخففة from أنْ المصدرية:\nIt follows a fi‘l al-qalb.\n\nIt doesn’t make the muḍāri‘ manṣūb.\n\nIt may precede a fi‘l jāmid (e.g. وأنْ ليس للإنسان إلا ما سعى).\n\nIt can enter on a jumlah ismiyyah (e.g. أنْ الحمد لله).\n\nWhen كأن is mukhaffafah:\nIt can still do ‘amal, and its ism can be mentioned or omitted (e.g. كأنْ ظبيةٌ تعطو…).\nWhen لكن is mukhaffafah:\nIt must not act — e.g. ولكنْ الشياطينُ كفروا.",
