        "overview": "In this video, we continue our discussion on ‘aṭf. ثُمَّ indicates sequence with delay—either in time or rank—and how it can show something far-fetched or stretched over a long period. حتى as a conjunctive particle, it is described as rare, with strict conditions and multiple grammatical possibilities.\nأم has two forms: connected (for specifying between two options after a hamzah) and disconnected (meaning بل or introducing a rhetorical shift). أو is explained as expressing choice, permissibility, uncertainty, or detail depending on context, with إما functioning similarly in some cases.\nThe particles بل, لكن, and لا are outlined with their respective roles: iḍrāb (shifting or cancelling), istidrāk (correcting an implied misunderstanding), and negation in ‘aṭf.\nTawkīd describes lafẓī repetition of a word, verb, particle, or sentence as a means of emphasis.",
