        "title": "Lesson 11 | The types of Kalimah",
        "overview": "The lesson discusses the concept of 'Taqseem' (categorization) and its importance in understanding the different types of 'Karima' (word). It explores the reasons for categorization and the perspectives from which categorization is done. Additionally, it delves into the difference between 'Kulli' and 'Kul' and the scientific method of 'Istiqra' (observation and conclusion). The discussion covers the concept of Istiqra and its types, the division of words into three categories, and the logic behind this categorization. It also delves into the definition and signs of each category, setting the stage for a deeper exploration in the next lesson.\n\nTakeaways\n- Taqseem (categorization) is essential for understanding the different types of 'Karima' (word).\n- The scientific method of 'Istiqra' involves observation and conclusion, leading to certainty. Istiqra is the process of drawing conclusions based on observation and evidence, leading to certainty or speculation.\n- Words are divided into three categories: Ism, Fial, and Harf, based on their ability to indicate meaning and tense.\n- The categorization of words into three types simplifies the understanding of their functionality and aids in comprehension.\n\nChapters\n- 00:00 The Scientific Method of Istiqra\n- 19:41 Understanding Istiqra and Its Types\n- 32:27 The Division of Words into Three Categories\n- 40:31 Exploring the Definition and Signs of Each Category",
