        "overview": "In this lesson, we examine one of the foundational discussions in Arabic grammar (naḥw): the distinction between المُعْرَب (al-muʿrab) and المَبْنِيّ (al-mabnī). This distinction lies at the heart of understanding how words function within a sentence and how meaning is conveyed through grammatical structure.\nThe discussion builds upon a previously established principle: that iʿrāb (الإِعْرَاب) exists to clarify the syntactic role of words. From this foundation, we explore why some words undergo grammatical change while others remain fixed, and what underlying wisdom governs these patterns.",
