        "overview": "This lesson continues the discussion on the construction (bināʾ) of the past tense verb (الفِعْلُ الْمَاضِي – al-fiʿlu al-māḍī) before introducing a group of exceptional words whose grammatical classification became a subject of disagreement among the classical grammarians. Ibn Hishām, in Sharḥ Qaṭr al-Nadā, not only explains the standard grammatical rules but also introduces students to areas of scholarly disagreement (خِلَاف – khilāf) between the schools of Baṣrah and Kūfah. This approach enables students to appreciate that Arabic grammar developed through rigorous scholarly debate rather than through a single unanimous tradition.\n\nAmong the words discussed are نِعْمَ, بِئْسَ, عَسَى, and لَيْسَ. The present lesson focuses on the first two: نِعْمَ and بِئْسَ.",
